  "meta": {
    "name": "mod-tools",
    "author": "I hope...",
    "description": "\nA mod provides various tools for modding.\n\n-----------------\nVersion 1.7.0\n\n## Highlight\n\n## New\n1. Deadlock detection watchdog: divergence heuristics for platform and virtual threads, JSON thread dumps, and a directed-graph cycle analysis that names the lock ring. Runs separately from the 5 ms CPU sampler so it cannot skew it.\n2. Review element editor: edit Element fields live to see the effect, no recompile needed.\n3. Layout check: LayoutIssues collects layout problems and LayoutReportWindow renders the report; cells also get a details window.\n4. Tester completion rewritten: member completion, array and object destructuring bindings, arrow parameter types from generic arguments; covered by JUnit 5.\n5. JS syntax highlighting for the Rhino editor, resolving members and generic types for accurate colouring.\n6. Zero-allocation float formatting: Schubfach shortest round-trip conversion, DoubleConversion and FastFormat, replacing Double.toString in Vec2/Vec3/Rect/Color formatting.\n\n## Hot swap\n7. Hot swap runs on a self-contained Remold agent, attached before settings load; a -javaagent setup that lacks plugin-arc now degrades with one warning instead of failing.\n8. UI hot swap: Table creator and Cell property chains are tracked, so a redefined builder rebuilds only the affected cells.\n9. Lambda and anonymous class alignment: LambdaAligner, AnonClassAligner and content-hash fingerprints keep anonymous classes paired across redefinition.\n10. Redefinition is gated on instance field-layout compatibility, and slot numbers held by pending aligned classes are not reused.\n11. The hotswap_plus switch is split into init_fix and force_static_lambda.\n\n## Performance\n12. ValueLabel, FieldValueLabel and InlineLabel format without boxing; PairProv shares one buffer and compares content before rebuilding.\n13. Flame graph: canvas clipping and culling, zero-allocation map lookups, spatial depth bucketing.\n14. Fewer per-frame allocations in LimitTable, SearchedLabel and completion prefix matching.\n15. Selection panel: dynamic region scanning is throttled to every 10 frames instead of running on a background executor; unit and bullet sets are cached between scans; tile and building icons are cached per block size.\n\n## Fixes\n\t- Completion popup not showing, and candidates beyond the first page being unreachable.\n\t- Completion popup covering the line being typed on.\n\t- changedFx flash overflowing the scroll pane viewport.\n\t- Viewers: Mat and Affine2 support, opening brace alignment in pretty print, and label markup state preserved across appends.\n\t- Android: HiddenApi trimmed in favour of the bundled bypass.\n\n## Dependencies\n\t- ASM 9.11 (security advisories), Remold 0.1.2.\n\n-----------------\nWIKI: https://i-hope1.github.io/mod-tools\n",
